                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for adding coverage for `afterGetUUID`!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joel Pullokaran Jesin",
                        "email": "joelpj@ami.com",
                        "username": "joel-pj"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the review and feedback! I've addressed the comments in the latest patch set."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/redfish-core/lib/system_test.cpp",
                    "line": 145,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Not sure if we can remove this line, since the next few lines already examine the full body of `response->res.jsonValue`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/redfish-core/lib/system_test.cpp",
                    "line": 145,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joel Pullokaran Jesin",
                        "email": "joelpj@ami.com",
                        "username": "joel-pj"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point. The subsequent full comparison already validating the complete response payload, including the top-level member count, so the explicit size check is redundant. I'll remove it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/redfish-core/lib/system_test.cpp",
                    "line": 162,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we have any smarter idea instead of hardcoding?\nOtherwise we might have to manually update the message body every time updating the version."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/redfish-core/lib/system_test.cpp",
                    "line": 162,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "As Ed has mentioned in the following link:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/92076/comment/2d35b369_1ac5a937/\n\nI think there is no more concern here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/redfish-core/lib/system_test.cpp",
                    "line": 232,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "I think we can do this to survives the registry bumps.\n\n```\ncrow::Response expected;\nmessages::internalError(expected);\nEXPECT_EQ(response->res.jsonValue, expected.jsonValue);\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/redfish-core/lib/system_test.cpp",
                    "line": 232,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Here as well."
                }
            ],
